Changes made by By Mel Ross (files carry a "Modified by By Mel Ross" or
"Added by By Mel Ross" note where they can hold a comment):
- Combined both projects into one skills folder and plugin (reel-editor sits in
  skills/3-editing/ beside edit-video); added skills/README.md, a guide to which
  skill to use when.
- reel-editor: gentle eased zooms by default, configurable in brand.json "zoom"
  (build_reel.py, auto_edit.py); configurable caption highlight shadow
  (build_reel.py); a Reel cover for every reel (new scripts/cover.py); delivery
  of a phone-size copy and the cover beside the full-quality file, optionally
  back to the footage folder (deliver.sh); a local review page for sessions
  without Artifact tools (new review/serve.mjs, references/review-local.md); a
  render option without "nice" (new scripts/render-nonice.sh, REEL_NO_NICE in
  render.sh and cut.py); ffmpeg 7+ filter-script flag (cut.py); HyperFrames
  pinned and telemetry off by default (render.sh, transcribe.py, tighten.py,
  qa.py, setup_engine.sh); doctor.sh finds HyperFrames skills kept outside the
  auto-loaded folder and checks for Chrome; SKILL.md, setup-interview.md and
  review.md updated to match.
- FavStash parts: plugin and package renamed to reel-studio; the remote FavStash
  connection is no longer added by the plugin (local only); validate-repo.mjs
  expects the reel-editor skill; AGENTS.md, INSTALL_FOR_AGENTS.md, README.md,
  CONTRIBUTING.md, SECURITY.md and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md rewritten or updated;
  edit-video/SKILL.md points to reel-editor for talking-head clips. FavStash's
  logo, social preview and style preview images (from its maintainer's own reels)
  are not included.
- Added brand/: the By Mel Ross example brand (brand.example.json,
  brand.example.md, style-reference.md) with the Lora and Inter fonts, which are
  licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 (license texts in brand/fonts/).
